# Accepted vulnerabilities need an id, a reason and a review date.
# Example:
# CVE-2024-00000  # expires 2026-12-01, no fixed release, not reachable in this service

# Open-source fixes for these three are Spring Framework 7.0.9 only.
# Review when the services move to Spring Boot 4.
# XsltView is not registered and there is no catch-all view resolver.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-02-17
# No server-sent event endpoint renders a fragment.
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-02-17
# WebFlux is used as a client. There is no functional router with a header predicate.
CVE-2026-47892 exp:2027-02-17

# The k3s node installs from the internet and pulls images, so egress stays open.
# Review if the node no longer needs outbound internet.
AVD-AWS-0104 exp:2027-02-17
# State and file buckets are private and encrypted with AES256.
# A customer managed key waits until the platform rotates keys itself.
AVD-AWS-0132 exp:2027-02-17
# Dev reuses image tags, so the registry module stays MUTABLE.
# Review when prod publishes immutable tags only.
AVD-AWS-0031 exp:2027-02-17
# The alert topic carries CPU and status alarms, not customer data.
# Review with the observability story.
AVD-AWS-0095 exp:2027-02-17
